From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:38:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): surface custody warnings in kanban_complete;
 drop executor-local attachment_path [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Live proof t_01a1d95bebb9b7a8 (home worker-8, executed worker-3) of PR #2910 showed two gaps:

1. The completing worker never saw its artifact_receipt warnings: the kanban_complete
   result carried only `attachments`, so a missing declared file ("File missing or not a
   regular file on executing machine") was silent until someone read the receipt.
   The result now also carries `artifact_receipt` and `artifact_warnings`
   (`machine:path — warning` lines) read from the completed event.

2. Receipt records stored `attachment_path`, the executor's flat
   `attachments/<task>/<name>` path, while the home keeps the bytes under
   `attachments/<task>/<attachment_uid>/<name>`. New receipts no longer store it
   (staging keeps the local mapping in a private dict); readers already resolve by
   attachment_id/attachment_uid. The legacy `artifacts` list keeps its executor-local
   path (executor-local consumers such as review handoff uploads read it), but the
   worker-context handoff display now machine-qualifies those paths (`worker-3:/...`) and
   hides `attachment_path` on older records. Old records are not rewritten.

Tests: tests/tools/test_kanban_complete_artifact_warnings.py (3 new) and the updated
receipt test fail on origin/main (4 failures) and pass here; 41 files importing the
touched modules: 891 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped. scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
